course: dictionary
lesson: 16007
title: Vocabulary in context: vaporise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Vaporise is a verb with three meanings, so the context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it and ask what they are about: heat, a ray, or a sudden disappearance?
explain: «The water in the pan began to boil, and soon it had vaporised into steam.» Heat turns water into steam, which is a gas. Here vaporise means to change from a liquid into a gas.
explain: «The laser vaporised the rock in a flash, and nothing was left.» Nothing was left, so the rock was destroyed completely. Here vaporise means to destroy something so that almost nothing remains.
explain: «The thief ran behind the wall and vaporised before anyone could see where he went.» Here vaporise is informal: the thief disappeared suddenly, as if into thin air. To check, swap in «disappeared» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Vaporise means to turn a liquid or a solid into a gas or vapour, usually by heating it.
fact: In science, sweat cools you because it vaporises from your skin.
fact: In stories, a ray or blast that vaporises something destroys it so completely that almost nothing is left.
fact: Related words are vapour, evaporate and vaporiser. In American spelling, it is written vaporize.
fact: The check works every time: put your meaning into the sentence and read it again.
exercise: «The heat vaporised the water in the kettle.» What does vaporised mean here? | Broke into tiny pieces | Turned into ice | Poured into a cup | *Turned into a gas
exercise: «The ray vaporised the old spaceship, and nothing was left.» What does vaporised mean here? | *Destroyed completely | Painted bright blue | Pushed gently aside
exercise: Sweat cools your body because it ____ from your skin. | Freezes | *Vaporises | Sings | Sinks
test: «The puddle vaporised slowly in the warm sun.» What does vaporised mean here? | *Changed into a gas and disappeared into the air | Turned to ice in the cold | Grew bigger and deeper | Was swept away by a river
test: Ben says, «The magician vaporised before our eyes!» What does he mean? | The magician turned into steam | The magician fell asleep on stage | *The magician disappeared suddenly | The magician grew taller
exam: What is a machine called that turns a liquid into a fine mist of vapour? | A vaporised ray | An evaporation | A vapour trail | *A vaporiser
